# Concerto smoke-gate capability manifest.
#
# One capability per line, in run order. Each <cap> maps to a file
# scripts/smoke.d/<NN>-<cap>.sh that the driver (scripts/smoke.sh) sources;
# that file must define a `check_<cap>` function (dashes -> underscores).
#
# Blank lines and `#`-comments are ignored. To extend the gate, a V1.0 task
# adds a scripts/smoke.d/<NN>-<newcap>.sh file and appends <newcap> here in
# the position it should run. Order matters: later checks depend on the
# PROJECT_ID -> REPO_ID -> WS_ID -> WA_ID -> SID chain built by earlier ones.
#
# Seeded with EXACTLY the V0.1 capabilities (net behavior unchanged).

core-boot
persistence-integrity
project-repo-clone
workspace-workarea
echo-session
streams-subscribe
files-transfer
permission-flip
audit-log
audit-rotation
loop
skills
mcp
cli
backup
connect-web-bridge
transport-loopback
mdns-discovery
relay-route
# Task 220: the Phase-2 capstone. Runs LAST — it boots its own Iroh-enabled
# Core (separate from the shared UDS smoke Core) + a synthetic paired device,
# and drives pair → IROH-tagged unary → Streams.Subscribe → Files up/down over
# two loopback Iroh endpoints (relays off). macOS-only at runtime; SKIPs cleanly
# on the ubuntu lane. (File prefix 94 is cosmetic; manifest order is authoritative,
# same as 46-relay-route running late.)
split-host-loopback
